# Loaded automatically by `next dev` (NODE_ENV=development) and takes
# precedence over .env. Committed on purpose — every value here is a public
# Cloudflare test constant, so a fresh clone gets working forms with no setup.
#
# Precedence, highest first:
#   .env.development.local  →  .env.local  →  .env.development  →  .env
# So to override any of this locally, put it in .env.local (gitignored).

# ── Cloudflare Turnstile — test keys ────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The campaign's real widget key is bound to the hostnames registered against
# it in the Turnstile dashboard, and `localhost` is not one of them. With the
# real key the widget mounts, Cloudflare rejects the hostname with error
# 110200, and the submit button never enables.
#
# These two always pass and work on any hostname. They are a MATCHED PAIR and
# must stay together: a test site key checked against the real secret passes in
# the browser and then fails siteverify server-side.
#
# Swap 1x → 2x to test the always-blocked path, or 3x for a forced interactive
# challenge. Cloudflare's full list:
# https://developers.cloudflare.com/turnstile/troubleshooting/testing/
NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=1x00000000000000000000AA
TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=1x0000000000000000000000000000000AA
